{"name":"Red Power","hex":"#d63d3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Red Power","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A social movement led by Native American youth to demand self-determination for Native Americans in the United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Red_Power"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Power movement","blocks":[{"text":"The Red Power movement was a social movement which was led by Native American youth who demanded self-determination for Native Americans in the United States. Organizations that were part of the Red Power Movement include the American Indian Movement (AIM) and the National Indian Youth Council (NIYC). This movement advocated the belief that Native Americans should have the right to implement their own policies and programs along with the belief that Native Americans should maintain and control their own land and resources. The Red Power movement took a confrontational and civil disobedience approach in an attempt to incite changes in Native American affairs in the United States compared to using negotiations and settlements, which national Native American groups such as National Congress of American Indians had before. Red Power centered around mass action, militant action, and unified action."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/American_Indian_Movement_Poster.jpg/330px-American_Indian_Movement_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Power_movement"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Representatives_of_various_tribes_attending_organizational_meeting_of_the_National_Congress_of_American_Indians..._-_NARA_-_298658.jpg/500px-Representatives_of_various_tribes_attending_organizational_meeting_of_the_National_Congress_of_American_Indians..._-_NARA_-_298658.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Representatives_of_various_tribes_attending_organizational_meeting_of_the_National_Congress_of_American_Indians..._-_NARA_-_298658.jpg/1280px-Representatives_of_various_tribes_attending_organizational_meeting_of_the_National_Congress_of_American_Indians..._-_NARA_-_298658.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Representatives_of_various_tribes_attending_organizational_meeting_of_the_National_Congress_of_American_Indians..._-_NARA_-_298658.jpg/500px-Representatives_of_various_tribes_attending_organizational_meeting_of_the_National_Congress_of_American_Indians..._-_NARA_-_298658.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1944 Meeting of National Congress of American Indians","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARepresentatives_of_various_tribes_attending_organizational_meeting_of_the_National_Congress_of_American_Indians..._-_NARA_-_298658.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Alcatraz_Occupation_%22Welcome_to_Indian_Land%22_graffiti.jpeg/500px-Alcatraz